From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:21:25 -0400
Subject: feat: Peek, rebuilt on the little window

Peek P1-P16 (BACKLOG S-93): a link from a pinned tab that leaves its site
opens in a peek, a little window over the pinned tab's window, nearly its
size (72 DIP at the sides, 48 at the top and bottom), and the pinned tab
stays where it was. The old overlay laid its page out 0 px tall and loaded
links as if typed, in the shared jar (PLAN.md CMD-9, CMD-10); it is gone,
with its keys.

The peek's page is a whole tab of a popup marked little, so dialogs, file
choosers, permissions, the popup blocker and the address row with the
site's security state work as in any tab. stedding::OpenPeek makes the page
in the pin's own jar (a pin in a Space with its own session peeks with that
session) and loads the link with its initiator, referrer, source site and
gesture; a page the source made itself (target=_blank, window.open) is
adopted as it is. A PeekPage on the page names the pin it came from and
watches the pin's window: a click on that window closes the peek, and when
the click lands on the very link the peek shows, the link does not open it
again. One peek over a window; the next link replaces it. The window's
bounds are set once it is made: the bounds a popup is made with were set
aside on the Mac. It shows with its page focused, so Escape closes it.

Only the user's click from the pin on screen peeks: the throttle and the
new-tab hook ask for a gesture and an active source tab. A redirect link is
judged by the http(s) address in its u=, q= or url=; a sign-in page (a
host such as login., accounts., sso.; a path step such as /login, /oauth,
/authorize, /saml) stays in the pin.

The peek's row has Open in Split View (Shift-Cmd-O, shown when the pin can
take a pair: not an essential, not a tab in a split) and Open as Tab
(Cmd-O); PromoteLittleWindow sends the page back to the pin's window and
Space, the mark taken off first. The page menu's first row says Open as
Tab in a peek. Settings > Stedding has the switch again, and Peek is on
by default (the owner, 2026-10-25; PLAN.md decision 2); the shortcut list
names the peek.
CreateLittleWindow is the little window without its page, shared by both,
and it sets the window's bounds once the window is made: the window sizer
had set the requested ones aside, so a little window opened at the last
window's size, 22 DIP down and right, never at most 1000 x 700 (little E1).

Why: Peek is what makes pinned tabs behave like apps, and it had been off
since its overlay showed no page and loaded links unsafely (PLAN.md
decision 2; the owner asked for the next big feature, 2026-10-24).
Removable when: never; it is product behaviour.
